<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis (Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica)",
        "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis faithfully reproduces Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cervera-levin-mafe-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cervera-levin-mafe-2> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 55.6/100, audit 2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    schema:about "Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Exact equation-by-equation identity with the paywalled Cervera et al. (2021) full text or continuous 2D/3D biomechanical tissue deformation",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 1D AP (m1, m2) and ML (m3) reaction-diffusion analogue coupled with a 5-node bistable V_mem circuit port from MesmerPrism/rusty-matter and PlanformDB 2.5.0 canonical silhouettes",
        "reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) model intercellular gap-junction blockade via effective diffusion reduction across AP (f2) and ML (f3) morphogen signals",
        "reported_in_source: Oviedo et al. (2010) and Durant et al. (2019) report crop-position-dependent double-head frequencies under octanol and triple-innexin RNAi and permanent two-headed regeneration after transient bioelectric depolarization",
        "transfer_boundary: One-parameter octanol crop-gradient calibration transferred to held-out triple-innexin RNAi crop frequencies" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py; output: cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif; organism: Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/a0d6848; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scipy 1.16.3, scikit-image 0.26.0; spec_fingerprint: ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc; artifact_sha256: 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/planform/planform_canonical_silhouettes_v1.json=cac26e64a315ed81...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-17-cervera-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) model intercellular gap-junction blockade via effective diffusion reduction across AP (f2) and ML (f3) morphogen signals | Oviedo et al. (2010) and Durant et al. (2019) report crop-position-dependent double-head frequencies under octanol and triple-innexin RNAi and permanent two-headed regeneration after transient bioelectric depolarization; reconstructed_in_script: 1D AP (m1, m2) and ML (m3) reaction-diffusion analogue coupled with a 5-node bistable V_mem circuit port from MesmerPrism/rusty-matter and PlanformDB 2.5.0 canonical silhouettes; transfer_boundary: One-parameter octanol crop-gradient calibration transferred to held-out triple-innexin RNAi crop frequencies; does_not_claim: Exact equation-by-equation identity with the paywalled Cervera et al. (2021) full text or continuous 2D/3D biomechanical tissue deformation]; other sources: Smediterranea.jpg, from A Low Percent Ethanol Method for Immobilizing Planarians <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Smediterranea.jpg>, MesmerPrism/rusty-matter planarian bioelectric circuit and fixtures <https://github.com/MesmerPrism/rusty-matter/tree/ad111fa7ecfd8f43d292ff3b1d27d3af2741d828>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bioelechem.2019.107410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biosystems.2021.104511>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2019.01.029>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.12.012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btt088> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Bioelectric Gap-Junction Coupled Nonlinear Dynamical Network" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 5.56e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Code-to-model traceability: 60/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The revision substantially improves internal traceability: model constants are centralized and disclaimed as local, f2 and f3 have one mapping each, fitting and held-out roles are explicit, every-sample parity is correctly scoped, and panel D admits its illustrative time rescaling. The phenotype number can be reconstructed from Planform geometry and renderer conventions. It is not, however, a source-derived biological criterion: the 100-unit pharynx length is a renderer constant, the denominator uses padded plotting bounds, and no paper supports the rule that passing this point creates a second head. Crop-specific circuit wound gains remain uncited, and the 2021 solver still cannot be traced to numbered source equations. Panel D's hard-coded legend values and pulse shading also disagree with current simulation output despite the improved title. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L27–L47: clear boundary between analogue, circuit port, criterion and silhouette measurement <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L27-L47>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L302–L338: centralized parameter mappings and reconstructible but uncited phenotype rule <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L302-L338>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L390–L415: silhouette extent used by the criterion contains 20-unit plotting padding <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L390-L415>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L526–L531: 100-unit pharynx length is a drawing convention, not an organ-table field <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L526-L531>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1262–L1305: time rescaling is acknowledged, but pulse span and legend percentages remain hard-coded and stale <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1262-L1305>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Model fidelity to source: 45/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cervera-levin-mafe-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cervera-levin-mafe-2> ;
    rdfs:comment "The program now accurately describes itself as a qualitative analogue built from the abstract and presentation, and explicitly disclaims equation, boundary-condition and parameter fidelity. Its high-level structure remains consistent with accessible source text: two antagonistic axial signals, an independent orthogonal signal and reduced effective diffusion under GJ block. f3 now genuinely changes D3 and an ML profile, replacing the false 2D heatmap with two honest independent curves. This still cannot score as a reproduction of the published model: the full 2021 paper was unavailable, the local solver docstring still says it implements the paper's system, no published equation or constants are verified, and m3 is not coupled to a morphological outcome. The rusty-matter port remains a separate unpublished educational model rather than the cited 2020 ion-channel model. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L27–L47: scope statement distinguishes qualitative analogue, educational port and measured silhouette <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L27-L47>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L213–L318: implemented AP and ML solvers, centralized constants and f2/f3 mappings <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L213-L318>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L230–L234: function docstring still attributes the unverified equations directly to Cervera 2021 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L230-L234>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1055–L1064: f3 now drives D3 and a nonconstant lateral index, explicitly independent of AP <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1055-L1064>; datasets/planform/README.md L21–L27: repository source boundary describes both mechanisms as qualitative or semi-quantitative abstractions <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/datasets/planform/README.md#L21-L27>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Morphometric validation: 48/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "This dimension has the clearest improvement. A one-parameter f2=1-a p model is fit to four octanol crop positions and evaluated, without refitting, against four innexin-RNAi positions; training RMSE is 4.2 points and held-out RMSE is 23.5 with r=0.94. The code reports these values in the figure and CSV, writes direct solver wavefronts, and measures anterior territory area on the photographic silhouette. This is a real model-data comparison rather than decorative anchors. It remains below the midpoint because four related positions are a very small validation set, no sampling uncertainty or baseline is reported, the 23.5-point held-out error is substantial, and the target is phenotype frequency while the predictor is a normalized signal-boundary index. The silhouette quantity is measured on a real body but is not compared with a measured treated specimen. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L997–L1018: one-parameter training and held-out evaluation, explicitly acknowledged as weak <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L997-L1018>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1048–L1053: direct x*, shift index and photographic-mask area are computed per crop <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1048-L1053>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1090–L1130: CSV contains direct wavefronts, fit metrics, f2 and f3 sweeps <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1090-L1130>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1207–L1259: panel C displays training and held-out metrics with empirical frequencies <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1207-L1259>; cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): regenerated table reports RMSE 4.2/23.5, r=0.94 and exact solver wavefronts — cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at a0d6848, text/csv, 5146 B, artifact_sha256 36e3036d0379d9fcb3bd1b4c646d04092c959c5ed03387d4937d8ac7d461afee (sha256 36e3036d0379d9fcb3bd1b4c646d04092c959c5ed03387d4937d8ac7d461afee), spec_fingerprint ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): rusty-matter trace parity, max |Δ| = 0.0332 state units (reference 0.0, MesmerPrism/rusty-matter commit ad111fa7ecfd8f43d292ff3b1d27d3af2741d828) [maximum absolute difference across all 5 scenarios, 11 sampled steps and 4 state averages against rusty_matter_planarian_traces.json]; symmetric RD wavefront x*(f2=1) = 0.5 AP fraction (reference 0.5, symmetric boundary conditions at x=0 and x=L) [zero crossing of m1(x) - m2(x) when D2 = D2_0]; pharynx-boundary criterion x*_b = 0.5833 AP fraction [posterior end of the Planform #1 wild-type pharynx on the AP extent] — crossed at f2_b = 0.4197 (where x*(f2_b) = 0.5833); anterior body-area fraction on S. mediterranea silhouette (f2=1 -> f2=0.25) = 0.1561 fraction of body area [increase in real-silhouette mask area anterior to x*(f2) from f2=1.0 (0.483) to f2=0.25 (0.639)]; ML centre/edge ratio λ(f3), f3=1.0 vs f3=0.3 = 0.1855 ratio difference (reference >0 (monotonic decrease under lateral gap-junction blockade)) [m3(L_z/2)/m3(0) drop from f3=1.0 (0.197) to f3=0.3 (0.011)]; Oviedo 2010 octanol crop-gradient training RMSE = 4.1871 percentage points (reference 0.0, PlanformDB 2.5.0 / Oviedo et al. 2010 Dev. Biol. 339:188) [1-parameter fit f2(p) = 1 - 0.58*p against Oviedo et al. 2010 octanol double-head frequencies (Exps 415-418, n=4 crops)]; Oviedo 2010 triple-innexin RNAi held-out RMSE = 23.5215 percentage points (reference 0.0, PlanformDB 2.5.0 / Oviedo et al. 2010 Dev. Biol. 339:188) [held-out prediction error of the octanol-fitted curve against Dj-Inx-12 + Dj-Inx-5/13 RNAi double-head frequencies (Exps 446-449, n=4 crops)] — Pearson r = 0.943; circuit posterior head readout, memory ON vs memory OFF control = 0.9185 readout [0,1] (reference 0.23491399812436778, TransientDepolarizationNoMemoryControl negative control (Durant et al. 2019 Biophys. J. 116:948)) [final posterior head-identity readout R_head,post under TransientDepolarizationMemory] — hysteresis memory sustains depolarised head fate after transient pulse ends; Planform #1 Wild Type vs #2 Double Head silhouette IoU = 0.9478 ratio (reference <1.0 (posterior tail replaced by ectopic head cap), PlanformDB 2.5.0 morphologies #1 and #2) [256x256 shared-canvas intersection-over-union of decoded Lobo et al. (2013) graph silhouettes]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-9> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — MorphoEval overall 55.6/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "A deterministic synthesis combines an explicitly labelled qualitative reaction–diffusion analogue, an orthogonal m3 profile, an educational rusty-matter circuit port, 14 curated PlanformDB records, a one-parameter crop-position fit and two fixed Planform cartoons. The additional outputs are cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png and cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv. The inert f3 and incorrect crop-wavefront defects are fixed, the silhouette is quantitatively sampled, and the empirical comparison now reports training and held-out errors. Remaining limits are the inaccessible full model papers, no f3-to-anatomy mapping, an uncited phenotype decision rule, weak held-out accuracy, fixed cartoon outcomes, illustrative time mapping and an incorrect reported f2 threshold caused by clipping in its inverse. Overall 55.6/100 (faithfulness 46.4, reproducibility 76.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a0d6848; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scipy 1.16.3, scikit-image 0.26.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 45, Morphological realism / specimen match 42, Parameter expressivity 58, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted). Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc; artifact_sha256: 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/planform/planform_canonical_silhouettes_v1.json=cac26e64a315ed81...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-17-cervera-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) model intercellular gap-junction blockade via effective diffusion reduction across AP (f2) and ML (f3) morphogen signals | Oviedo et al. (2010) and Durant et al. (2019) report crop-position-dependent double-head frequencies under octanol and triple-innexin RNAi and permanent two-headed regeneration after transient bioelectric depolarization; reconstructed_in_script: 1D AP (m1, m2) and ML (m3) reaction-diffusion analogue coupled with a 5-node bistable V_mem circuit port from MesmerPrism/rusty-matter and PlanformDB 2.5.0 canonical silhouettes; transfer_boundary: One-parameter octanol crop-gradient calibration transferred to held-out triple-innexin RNAi crop frequencies; does_not_claim: Exact equation-by-equation identity with the paywalled Cervera et al. (2021) full text or continuous 2D/3D biomechanical tissue deformation." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Calibrate or remove the illustrative 24-hour circuit overlay, generate legend values and pulse bounds from the simulation, and either source or remove the crop-specific rusty-matter wound-gain lookup.",
        "remediation needed: Fix f2_for_shift so it solves wavefront_for_f2(f2) = x_star_b without a clipped objective, test the recovered crossing, and correct the CSV/panel value from 0.20 to the actual approximately 0.42.",
        "remediation needed: Map f3 to a measured lateral morphology such as auricle width or head shape and compare it with specimens or source figures; otherwise describe f3 only as signal-profile expressivity.",
        "remediation needed: Obtain the full 2021 paper and map the analogue against its actual equations, boundary conditions, blocker factors and parameter definitions; retain the analogue label for every unmatched element.",
        "remediation needed: Replace the pharynx-crossing decision rule with a cited or empirically tested morphogen-to-phenotype mapping; if retaining this geometry, use actual body-mask bounds and state explicitly that the rule itself is an assumption.",
        "remediation needed: Validate the crop model on more independent experiments, include sampling uncertainty and simple baselines, and explain whether a 23.5-point held-out RMSE is adequate for the intended claim." ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.56e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Parameter expressivity: 58/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Both named reaction–diffusion factors now have visible monotonic effects across stated sweeps: decreasing f2 advances x* and the silhouette's anterior area share, while decreasing f3 sharply lowers the ML centre/edge concentration ratio. The self-test asserts both monotonic f2 response and a non-inert f3 range, and panel E shows the profiles rather than a misleading 2D surface. Credit is limited because f3 changes only an independently normalized concentration curve and is never translated into lateral head or auricle form; morphology remains a binary cartoon switch. The circuit's crop-specific wound gains also remain a fixed lookup rather than an independently tested parameterization. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L302–L318: single definitions of f2 wavefront and f3 centre/edge index <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L302-L318>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L965–L973: f2 sweep computes both wavefront and real-mask area share <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L965-L973>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1055–L1064: f3 sweep produces nonconstant ML profiles and lambda values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1055-L1064>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1310–L1337: panel E visibly presents the two independent parameter curves <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1310-L1337>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1422–L1428: self-test checks f2 monotonicity and f3 sensitivity <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1422-L1428>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Reproducibility package: 84/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The environment exactly matched the recorded Python and five package versions, dependencies are locked, inputs are hash checked, and two complete runs produced byte-identical PNG, CSV and 46-frame GIF. The expanded self-test checks symmetry, f2 monotonicity, f3 sensitivity and every crop CSV wavefront, while port parity now compares all 11 frames and four state fields for every scenario and accurately says this is not biological validation. The package is held below a higher score because the test only checks that the fit metrics are finite, not correct; it misses the f2 inverse defect that prints 0.20 instead of the approximately 0.42 crossing; and it does not verify stale panel-D labels. The full prescribed repeat also took about 12.5 minutes, mostly because self-test renders the complete analysis figure. Evidence: requirements.lock.txt L18–L41: tested scientific dependencies are pinned <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/requirements.lock.txt#L18-L41>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L700–L770: hash verification and all-frame, all-field port parity <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L700-L770>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1412–L1442: expanded self-test, including CSV recomputation but no assertion of expected fit or inverse threshold <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1412-L1442>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L341–L351: clipped target inversion returns the lower bound for target=1 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L341-L351>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1537–L1587: headless-capable CLI and correctly scoped self-test output <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1537-L1587>; cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): regenerated byte-identically in two independent runs — cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at a0d6848, image/png, 547708 B, 2330×1781 px, artifact_sha256 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77 (sha256 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77), spec_fingerprint ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc; cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): regenerated byte-identically with direct solver wavefronts — cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at a0d6848, text/csv, 5146 B, artifact_sha256 36e3036d0379d9fcb3bd1b4c646d04092c959c5ed03387d4937d8ac7d461afee (sha256 36e3036d0379d9fcb3bd1b4c646d04092c959c5ed03387d4937d8ac7d461afee), spec_fingerprint ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Source and data traceability: 82/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Source and data traceability was already strong: papers have resolvable DOIs, rusty-matter is pinned to a full commit, fixtures and photograph have SHA-256 values, and PlanformDB-derived records retain experiment IDs and sample counts. The previously wrong 2021 PMID is corrected to 34411690, and the script now records exactly which source material was and was not consulted. It also labels fitted versus held-out empirical series. Remaining limits are that the full 2021 and 2020 papers were not accessible and the raw PlanformDB was not independently re-extracted, so the curated fixture transcription and equation provenance remain unverified. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L6–L47: correct PMID, source DOIs and explicit scope/source-access boundary <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L6-L47>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L98–L130: fixture and photograph hashes, URL, species and credit <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L98-L130>; datasets/planform/README.md L1–L19: PlanformDB pin, notice, upstream commit, fixture hashes and experiment groups <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/datasets/planform/README.md#L1-L19>; datasets/planform/rusty_matter_planformdb_derived_v0.json L1–L39: database identity, raw checksum, citations and selection policy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/datasets/planform/rusty_matter_planformdb_derived_v0.json#L1-L39>; datasets/planform/paper_citations.bib L29–L80: bibliographic records for model and empirical sources <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/datasets/planform/paper_citations.bib#L29-L80>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Morphological realism / specimen match: 42/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The real Schmidtea silhouette is now used for an area measurement as well as a backdrop, and the regenerated figure is more legible than the previous version. Wild type and double head remain visibly distinct. But the body outline never changes, no real treated or double-head specimen or source-paper morphology is shown, and the model does not generate head or auricle form. Crossing a threshold merely swaps between two pre-existing Planform cartoons; measuring coloured territory area improves quantification, not anatomical realism. Thus the central specimen-match requirement remains mostly unmet. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L150–L207: photograph is segmented into the fixed mask on which signals are painted <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L150-L207>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L354–L362: new morphometric is the mask area lying anterior to the one-dimensional signal crossing <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L354-L362>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L795–L869: outcomes remain fixed WT and double-head Planform graph cartoons <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L795-L869>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1511–L1519: GIF threshold selects one of the two cartoons rather than deforming anatomy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1511-L1519>; cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): regenerated six-panel figure is legible but contains no real phenotype comparison — cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at a0d6848, image/png, 547708 B, 2330×1781 px, artifact_sha256 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77 (sha256 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77), spec_fingerprint ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

